` if using Tiptap; enables direct `editor.chain().focus().toggleBold()` etc.\n- **or** action callbacks (if editor instance shouldn’t be passed):  \n  - `onToggleBold`, `onToggleItalic`, `onToggleUnderline`, `onToggleHeading`, `onToggleBulletList`, `onToggleNumberedList`, `onUndo`, `onRedo`\n- UI state flags for active formatting (if not using `editor.isActive`):  \n  - `isBoldActive`, `isItalicActive`, `isUnderlineActive`, `activeHeadingLevel`, `isBulletListActive`, `isNumberedListActive`\n- Optional feature toggles:  \n  - `showEditorTools?: boolean` and `onToggleEditorTools?: (next: boolean) => void` (fits the toolbar toggle pattern in this codebase)\n\nIf you’re already using a shared editor hook/store, I can map the exact fields for you, but I’ll need to know which editor component manages formatting state.\n\nWhich editor implementation is used in this builder (Tiptap `Editor`, a custom Markdown editor, or something else), and do you prefer passing the `editor` instance or explicit callbacks?\n</summary>\n</subagent_invocation>"}
