2026-04-04 10:59:21.681 | 655960 (655960) | DEBUG    | Model request part: {"tool_name": "invoke_subagents", "content": "<subagent_invocation>\n<subagent>\nSubagent: Next.js 15 AI Development Assistant (selection-hud-plan)\n</subagent>\n\n<task_description>\nPlan how to show SelectionGenerationHUD when text selected in editor. Check useEditorStore selection state and existing generation HUD patterns in src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/generation. Provide concise guidance on implementation and where to wire it.\n</task_description>\n\n<notes>\n\n</notes>\n\n<summary>\nHere\u2019s a concise implementation plan based on the current editor store + generation HUD patterns:\n\n**1) Extend editor selection state (needed for reactive HUD visibility).**  \n`useEditorStore` currently only tracks formatting flags, not whether text is selected. Add fields such as:\n- `hasSelection: boolean`\n- `selectionText: string`\n- `selectionLength: number`\n- optionally `selectionRange: { from: number; to: number }`\n\nUpdate `updateSelectionState(editor)` to compute these from `editor.state.selection`. This keeps the HUD reactive without probing the editor directly.\n\n**2) Ensure selection changes update the store.**  \nIn `MarkdownEditor.tsx`, `updateSelectionState` only runs inside `onUpdate` (content change). To reflect pure selection changes, call it in `onSelectionUpdate` too (alongside the heading detection logic). This is critical for showing/hiding the HUD when the user selects text but doesn\u2019t type.\n\n**3) Add `SelectionGenerationHUD` in `builder/generation/`.**  \nFollow the same structure and styling as `SectionGenerationHUD`/`ChapterGenerationHUD` (same file area and aesthetic).  \nInside the HUD:\n- read `selection` + `activeEditor` from `useEditorStore`\n- early return `null` if `!selection.hasSelection`\n- use `selectionText` for preview context (or `activeEditor.state.doc.textBetween(...)` if you prefer direct access)\n- hook actions using `useAiActions({ editor: activeEditor ?? undefined })`\n\n**4) Wire the HUD where it belongs.**  \nTwo good options\u2014pick one based on UX:\n\n**A. Right sidebar panel (matches current generation HUD pattern):**  \n- Add a new panel in `useSidebarPanels.tsx`, e.g. `{ key: 'selection', title: 'Selection Tools', content: <SelectionGenerationHUD /> }`.\n- In `BuilderWorkspace` (or `useReportGenerator`), use `useEditorStore` to detect `hasSelection` and call `setActiveRightPanelKey('selection')` when true; revert to `'section'` when false.\n\n**B. Floating overlay in the canvas:**  \n- Render `<SelectionGenerationHUD />` as an absolute overlay inside `BuilderCanvas` (similar to the Zoom HUD pattern).  \n- This keeps it near the content and avoids sidebar switching. Use `absolute top-6 right-6 z-40` + glassmorphism classes similar to other HUDs.\n\n**Recommendation:** Start with **Option A** (sidebar) to align with current generation tools UX and reduce layout complexity; move to overlay if you want faster \u201cinline AI\u201d feel.\n\nWould you like me to draft the actual `SelectionGenerationHUD` component and the store/MarkdownEditor wiring, or just outline the sidebar/overlay wiring in more detail?\n</summary>\n</subagent_invocation>", "tool_call_id": "call_85M6b5l9GYS8osOYnFo7LcTj", "metadata": null, "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:59:21.680292+00:00", "part_kind": "tool-return"}
